Replaced the linear scan with a one-time-built 65536-entry pointer table keyed by message number, preserving the first match for duplicates and NULL for misses. This makes each lookup O(1) instead of O(MESGS).

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const MESG* table[65536] = {};
    static const bool initialized = []() {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; ++i)
        {
            if (table[mesgs[i].num] == NULL)
                table[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        return true;
    }();
    (void)initialized;
    return table[num];
}
```